  "notes": "{散|ち}らす means to scatter or spread things in different directions.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {散|ち}る (intransitive, to scatter by itself)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{散|ち}らしている indicates things are scattered about or that scattering is ongoing.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {花|はな}びらを{散|ち}らす: to scatter petals\n- {気|き}を{散|ち}らす: to distract (someone's mind)\n- {注意|ちゅうい}を{散|ち}らす: to distract attention\n- ばらばらに{散|ち}らす: to scatter everywhere\n\nRELATED:\n{散|ち}らかす: to make a mess, leave things scattered",
